      <div class="split__body prose">
        <p class="rv">AI agent cybersecurity testing evaluates autonomous AI agents for security weaknesses that could allow attackers to manipulate agent behavior or trigger unauthorized actions. Testing focuses on risks such as indirect prompt injection and excessive permissions along with insecure tool integrations and unauthorized data access.</p>
        <p class="rv">AI agents introduce new cybersecurity risks because they can interpret instructions and interact with APIs or external tools while accessing sensitive business data. Security weaknesses such as prompt injection and excessive permissions can manipulate agent behavior or trigger unauthorized actions. CipherTrivia provides AI agent cybersecurity testing to identify vulnerabilities in agent workflows and evaluate the effectiveness of security controls.</p>
        <p class="rv">Our AI agent security testing assesses agent permissions and tool integrations along with authentication mechanisms and data access boundaries. We simulate relevant attack scenarios to identify risks such as unauthorized tool execution and indirect prompt injection as well as sensitive data exposure and privilege escalation. Our testing findings include risk-based recommendations to help organizations strengthen AI agent security and reduce the likelihood of exploitation across connected systems.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
